# Haratna environment variables
#
# The app currently has ZERO runtime dependency on environment variables —
# every "backend" call is served by the local mock service layer
# (src/services/*), so `npm install && npm start` works with no .env file
# at all. This file exists to establish the convention *before* real
# backend integration starts, not because anything here is wired up yet.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values once a real backend/service
# exists. Never commit a real `.env` file — it's already gitignored.
#
# Expo only exposes variables prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ to client bundles
# (web, iOS, Android) — anything without that prefix stays server-side
# only and is never bundled. That boundary is what keeps privileged
# secrets (a Supabase service-role key, APNs private keys, signing
# credentials, etc.) out of the app the way client-visible config
# never should carry them.

# --- Client-visible (EXPO_PUBLIC_*) — safe to ship in the app bundle ---

# Example future values, once a real backend replaces src/services/*:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# --- Server-side / build-time only — NEVER prefix these EXPO_PUBLIC_ ---
# (used only by scripts/*.mjs or a future backend deploy — never read by
# the app itself)

# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# APNS_PRIVATE_KEY=
